sections.template:
RENT AGREEMENT

This Rent Agreement is executed at {execution_place} on {execution_date}

BETWEEN

{applicant_name}
R/o {applicant_address}
PAN: {applicant_pan}
(Hereinafter referred to as the "LANDLORD" which expression shall include his/her heirs, executors, administrators, and assigns)

AND

{respondent_name}
R/o {respondent_address}
PAN: {respondent_pan}
(Hereinafter referred to as the "TENANT" which expression shall include his/her heirs, executors, administrators, and assigns)

sections.prompt_context:
Generate 12-18 numbered clauses for a residential rent agreement. This is a LEGAL CONTRACT — tone should be formal and precise. Use the following details:
- Property: {property_address}, measuring {property_area_sqft} sq. ft., for {property_type} use
- Tenure: {tenure_months} months from {lease_start_date} to {lease_end_date}
- Rent: Rs. {rent_amount}/- ({rent_amount_words}) per month, due on {rent_due_date}, payable via {payment_mode}
- Annual escalation: {escalation_percent}%
- Security deposit: Rs. {security_deposit}/- ({security_deposit_words}), refundable on vacating (less deductions)
- Notice period: {notice_period_months} months for termination by either party
- Permitted use: {permitted_use}
- Maintenance: {maintenance_responsibility}

Must include clauses on: (1) Grant of tenancy and tenure, (2) Rent and due date, (3) Security deposit terms and refund conditions, (4) Escalation, (5) Maintenance and repairs, (6) Permitted use, (7) Sub-letting prohibition, (8) Structural alterations, (9) Termination and notice period, (10) Consequences of default, (11) Force majeure, (12) Dispute resolution (jurisdiction). Additional terms if any: {facts_narrative}. Do NOT generate signature block — that is template-handled.
